rados-nkv target/ — KV bdev forwarder (out-of-tree against UNMODIFIED SPDK)
==========================================================================

Build knobs we own (NOT SPDK's)
-------------------------------

These sources build against an UNMODIFIED SPDK (Gerrit 28298 + memory_domain),
which has no Mercury support. So the Mercury (inter-tier RPC) build knob is OURS,
not SPDK's generated spdk/config.h:

  NKVX_WITH_MERCURY
      Gates the Mercury front-bridge code paths (kvdev_rados_nkvx_front.{c,h} and
      every call site in bdev_kvrados.c). Define it by passing -DNKVX_WITH_MERCURY
      from the build (target/Makefile, and the umbrella rados-nkvx/Makefile — those
      Makefiles land in later slices E/F). Without the macro, the forwarder builds
      as a stock, Mercury-less module that is byte-identical to upstream.

      Replaces the former in-tree SPDK_CONFIG_* mercury macro, which only existed
      because Mercury support used to be compiled into our SPDK fork via
      `./configure --with-mercury`. In the out-of-tree world there is no such fork.

  NKVX_WITH_WASM
      Gates the dlopen-backed wasmtime Exec runtime in kvdev_rados_nkvx_wasm.c.
      Define it by passing -DNKVX_WITH_WASM from the build (the executor's
      rados-nkvx/Makefile, which IS the real-wasm runtime, and the kvdev unit-test
      mk target/test/kvdev_rados_nkvx_ut.mk). Without the macro the wasm core
      collapses to its NOT_SUPPORTED stub and real KV-Exec returns -7. libwasmtime.so
      is dlopen'd lazily at runtime from /usr/local/lib (no link dependency); the
      wasmtime C-API headers under target/wasmtime/include supply only signatures.

      Replaces the former in-tree SPDK_CONFIG_* wasm macro, which only existed because
      WASM support used to be compiled into our SPDK fork via `./configure
      --with-wasm`. In the out-of-tree world (UNMODIFIED SPDK) there is no such knob,
      so the wasm core gates on OUR macro instead (Slice K, parallel to
      NKVX_WITH_MERCURY).
